<title>POLAND: Poland sells PLN 76.6 mln of 3-yr bond to public.</title>
<headline>Poland sells PLN 76.6 mln of 3-yr bond to public.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish treasury sold 76.6 million zlotys of Polish three-year index-linked bonds to the public in the February 3 to February 20 period, the finance ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bonds come from a 400 million zloty tranche of the three-year paper due February 6, 2000, which is to be offered to the public until April 30, 1997. The issue price was 99.50.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
